  "lineage": "Urban popular music of Yerevan that grew in the 1970s and 1980s among singers performing at weddings, restaurants and celebrations, setting Armenian songs in the ornamented vocal style and dance rhythms shared with the wider Middle Eastern and Caucasian city tradition. The name is usually traced to rabis, the Soviet abbreviation for art workers; the style spread on cassette, at concerts and later on video.",
